-- ============================================================================
-- EC1 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Cash Flow & NPV, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: TIME. The discount rate and its two conventions,
-- real against nominal and the Fisher rate that joins them, the valuation
-- year and what "sunk" does to a row, NPV and its profile, discounted
-- payback, DPI and discounted take, the internal rate of return with its
-- Newton-then-bisection root finder and its four null shapes, and the
-- sweeps of price, discount rate and decline that end in the breakeven
-- price. It ends knowing that IRR is a property of a curve, not of a
-- project.
--
-- ON THE REAL BASIS WITH THE ESCALATORS SET, NPV DOES NOT MOVE WITH
-- INFLATION, and that is the shape of the tier. AKATA reports NPV
-- 72534830.66 at 0, 1, 2, 3, 5 and 8 percent inflation while its real
-- total net cash flow falls from 141637829.18 to 83912631.29 and the
-- applied real rate falls from 10.000000 to 1.851852 percent: the Fisher
-- relation deflates the flows and the rate together and the two cancel.
-- The convention that DOES move NPV is mid-year against end-year,
-- 72534830.66 against 70188970.32 on the same rows, which is why the
-- capstone grades both.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A cash flow with a terminal negative has
-- two rates that zero its NPV, and irr() reports whichever root Newton
-- reaches from 10 percent with no flag. The published vector
-- [-100, 208, -108.12] is zero at 2.0000 and at 6.0000 percent; the engine
-- reports 6.0000 and the oracle 2.0000. AKATA with a 60000000 abandonment
-- reports 23.2570 percent; with 200000000 it reports null.
--
-- THE RECORDED ENGINE DEFECT THIS TIER OWNS. The NPV profile's applied-rate
-- point is evaluated at the rate ROUNDED TO TWO DECIMALS, so on a real basis
-- whose Fisher rate is 6.796117 percent the point labelled 6.8 reads
-- 72513070.98 against a headline of 72534830.66 on AKATA, a gap of
-- -21759.68, and -40996.42 on the published multiyear_pia_real case. The
-- header says the curve always passes through the headline. It does not.
--
-- The numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the discounted
-- readings and the knowledge that every one of them names a convention.
-- ============================================================================

values ('cashflow', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-why-time-matters","title":"Why Time Matters","lesson_keys":["l01-a-dollar-next-year","l02-what-the-discount-rate-is","l03-end-year-and-mid-year","l04-what-a-convention-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m02-real-and-nominal","title":"Real and Nominal","lesson_keys":["l01-inflation-in-the-ledger","l02-the-fisher-rate","l03-the-same-field-on-two-bases","l04-the-valuation-year","l05-sunk-years"]},{"key":"m03-net-present-value","title":"Net Present Value","lesson_keys":["l01-npv-row-by-row","l02-the-npv-profile","l03-discounted-payback","l04-dpi-and-the-index-it-is-not","l05-take-discounted-and-not"]},{"key":"m04-the-internal-rate-of-return","title":"The Internal Rate of Return","lesson_keys":["l01-what-irr-solves","l02-newton-and-bisection","l03-when-there-is-no-irr","l04-when-there-are-two","l05-what-irr-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m05-sweeps","title":"Sweeps","lesson_keys":["l01-the-price-sweep","l02-the-discount-rate-sweep","l03-the-breakeven-price","l04-the-decline-sweep"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
